dcat_catalog_compact_graph_page1.json   https://data.public.lu/api/1/site/catalog.jsonld?page=1&page_size=5  HTTP 200
    COMPACT JSON-LD: one object, "@context" (an @vocab of dcat# plus prefixed term definitions) + "@graph" (51 nodes:
    5 datasets' distributions and checksums, and the Catalog / hydra:Collection node). Written without indentation, every
    node verbatim. The hydra statement says 100 per page, 3210 datasets (the page_size=5 query only shortened this page).
    Candidates tried in the brief's order for "an EU CKAN portal that answers /catalog.jsonld with @context + @graph";
    NONE of the ckanext-dcat portals did (a ckanext-dcat catalog answers an expanded, flattened array, like data.gov.ie):
      https://dati.gov.it/catalog.jsonld            404 (HTML)
      https://datos.gob.es/catalog.jsonld           404
      https://data.overheid.nl/catalog.jsonld       404 (HTML)
      https://www.data.gv.at/catalog.jsonld         404
      https://opendata.swiss/catalog.jsonld?page=1  200 application/ld+json, a FLATTENED array (no @context/@graph)
      https://ckan.opendata.swiss/catalog.jsonld    200, flattened (the same)
      https://data.gov.gr/catalog.jsonld            200, flattened
      https://data.gov.ro/catalog.jsonld            200, flattened
      https://open.canada.ca/data/catalog.jsonld    200, flattened
      https://data.gov.sk, data.gov.hr, data.norge.no, avaandmed.eesti.ee: 200 but text/html (not a feed)
      data.public.lu, www.data.gouv.fr, dados.gov.pt (udata portals, not CKAN): 200 compact @graph  <- recorded: Luxembourg
    So this fixture is an EU portal on udata, not CKAN. The CKAN adapter's twin of it is opendata.swiss (listed in the
    seeds as one portal through two adapters).

pod_data_json_with_distributions.json   https://healthdata.gov/data.json  HTTP 200 application/json
    Project Open Data data.json with "distribution" arrays; one dataset carries a licence URI
    (https://open.fda.gov/license) and "accrualPeriodicity": "R/P1Y". TRUNCATED: the catalog envelope plus the first 20
    entries of "dataset" (the full file is ~31 MB, 31,319,575 bytes), cut by parsing the first 1.2 MB of the stream; the 20
    entries are verbatim. Written without indentation.
    The owner's "HHS" address https://www.hhs.gov/data.json answered HTTP 403 "Access Denied" (an Akamai block) to
    this client, to curl's default agent and over http; it was not retried with another identity. healthdata.gov is HHS's
    own health data portal and answered 200, so it is the recorded feed; the seeds list www.hhs.gov as failed.

